{"availability":"available","full":"tediko/ip-address-tracker","name":"ip-address-tracker","description":"IP Address Tracking app using two separate APIs together.","category":"Developer tools","language":"SCSS","stars":2,"forks":2,"created":"2021-05-03T11:12:46Z","updated":"2021-05-16T14:51:26Z","branch":"master","homepage":"https://iptracker-tediko.netlify.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://iptracker-tediko.netlify.app/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:41.039Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:41.039Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:41.039Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T21:05:41.039Z","stars":2,"forks":2}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Hello! This is my solution to IP address tracker - Frontend Mentor. Im surprised how much I learned from a seemingly easy challenge. I ran into problems with CORS on firefox and lost a lot of time trying to figure it out. For the first time I used webpack, environment variables and object literals.","⭐Featured solution in Vol. 54 of the Frontend Mentor Newsletter."],"features":["This is first time I used webpack. More specifically i used laravel mix which is a wrapper for webpack and targets the 80% usecase. I didn't realize how powerful tool it is.","Implement an environment variable for my APIKEY. This is a variable whose value is set outside the program to secure our sensitive data. I did it with serverless Lambda functions on netlify, so my APIKEY never shows up…","This is first time I used object literals instead of if statement in Tracker.changeContent function. Shortly, we have an object where the keys are the conditions and the values are the responses. Then we can use the…","Added aria-live=\"polite\" and aria-atomic=\"true\" to my .trackerresults-wrapper element to expose dynamic content changes in a way that can be announced by assistive technologies after my results inner elements change…","I didn't like that results container with address informations cover the map and user can't do anything with that. Added button to hide that container. More useful on mobile tho."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tediko/ip-address-tracker/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"3b0df816e66ce55970ce6f735fb81fcb8402abd2dc5c4f2078c21c905dc1abd9","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:41.179Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:41.179Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Hello! This is my solution to IP address tracker - Frontend Mentor. Im surprised how much I learned from a seemingly easy challenge. I ran into problems with CORS on firefox and lost a lot of time trying to figure it out. For the first time I used webpack, environment variables and object literals.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tediko/ip-address-tracker/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"3b0df816e66ce55970ce6f735fb81fcb8402abd2dc5c4f2078c21c905dc1abd9","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tediko/ip-address-tracker/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:41.180Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2021-05-16T14:51:26Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tediko/ip-address-tracker/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:41.180Z","hash":"3b0df816e66ce55970ce6f735fb81fcb8402abd2dc5c4f2078c21c905dc1abd9","originalBytes":5281,"storedBytes":5281,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["address","api","frontend","object","tracker","used","challenge","first","intro","key","mentor","netlify","problems","proxy","time","user","using","webpack","any","between","design","didn","environment","features","get","how","like","link","links","map","overview","page","request","see","useful","value","added","after","app","because","built","challenge.","cors","data","data.","elements","fetch","fetching","firefox","function","geolocation","hide","implement","info","keys","lambda","leafletjs","literals","mobile","out","preview","process","resources","results","server","serverless"